/* =========================================================
   ITEMS DATA
   Content for the "Items" dropdown in the Reference pane --
   Equipment (all non-magical gear) and, eventually, Magic Items.
   Same {intro, entries:[{id, title, html, children?}]} shape as
   LORE_DATA / SPELLS_DATA / CLASSES_DATA / FEATS_DATA. dm-screen.js
   reads this and builds the actual dropdown elements on page load
   via renderDataDrivenReferenceSections().

   STATUS: Equipment complete. Magic Items still to come.
   ========================================================= */

const ITEMS_DATA = {"intro":"","entries":[{"id":"items-equipment","title":"Equipment","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-weapons","title":"Weapons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-weapon-properties","title":"Weapon Properties","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-property-ammunition","title":"Ammunition","html":"<p>A weapon with this property needs ammunition to make a ranged attack — the required ammo type is listed alongside its range. Each attack expends one piece; drawing it from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack itself (a one-handed weapon still needs a free hand to load). After a fight, spending a minute searching the battlefield recovers half the ammunition used, rounded down — the rest is lost, broken, or unrecoverable.</p><p>Trying to use an Ammunition weapon for a melee attack instead works, but it's treated as an improvised weapon.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-finesse","title":"Finesse","html":"<p>A Finesse weapon can use either Strength or Dexterity for both its attack roll and damage roll — the wielder's choice, but the same score for both rolls on a given attack. This is what lets a Dexterity-based fighter use a rapier or dagger just as effectively as a Strength-based one.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-heavy","title":"Heavy","html":"<h5>New Rules (2024)</h5><p>You have Disadvantage on attack rolls with a Heavy weapon unless your Strength score is at least 13 (for a Melee weapon) or your Dexterity score is at least 13 (for a Ranged weapon).</p><h5>Legacy Rules (2014)</h5><p>Small creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls made with a Heavy weapon.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-light","title":"Light","html":"<p>Taking the Attack action and attacking with a Light weapon lets you make one extra attack later on the same turn as a Bonus Action, using a different Light weapon in your other hand. That bonus-action attack doesn't add your ability modifier to its damage unless that modifier is negative — the classic two-weapon fighting combo (e.g. a shortsword in one hand, a dagger in the other) runs on this property.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-loading","title":"Loading","html":"<p>A Loading weapon can only fire a single piece of ammunition each time you use an action, Bonus Action, or Reaction to fire it — no matter how many attacks a feature would otherwise let you make with it. It's the mechanical reason hand crossbows don't just let you fire twice per Attack action at low level.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-range","title":"Range","html":"<p>Shown as two numbers in feet next to the Ammunition or Thrown property (short/long). Attacking a target beyond the first number gives you Disadvantage on the attack roll; you simply can't attack a target beyond the second number at all.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-reach","title":"Reach","html":"<p>Adds 5 feet to your reach whenever you attack with this weapon, and to your reach for Opportunity Attacks made with it — letting you threaten a 10-foot radius instead of the usual 5 feet.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-thrown","title":"Thrown","html":"<p>A Thrown weapon can be hurled to make a ranged attack, and you can draw it as part of that same attack. If it's normally a melee weapon, you still use whichever ability modifier you'd use for a melee attack with it (so a thrown dagger can use Dexterity, since it's also Finesse, while a thrown handaxe uses Strength).</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-two-handed","title":"Two-Handed","html":"<p>Simply requires both hands to attack with it — no versatility, no one-handed option.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-property-versatile","title":"Versatile","html":"<p>Can be wielded in one hand or two. The damage value in parentheses next to the property is what it deals when used two-handed for a melee attack; the main damage entry is what it deals one-handed.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-weapon-mastery-properties","title":"Weapon Mastery Properties","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-mastery-cleave","title":"Cleave","html":"<p>Hitting a creature with a melee attack using this weapon lets you make a melee attack roll with the same weapon against a second creature within 5 feet of the first (and within your own reach). On a hit, the second creature takes the weapon's damage, but you don't add your ability modifier to that damage unless the modifier is negative. Usable once per turn.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-graze","title":"Graze","html":"<p>If your attack roll with this weapon misses, you still deal damage equal to the ability modifier you used to make the attack — same damage type as the weapon. That damage can only be increased by increasing the ability modifier itself (no bonus dice apply).</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-nick","title":"Nick","html":"<p>Lets the Light property's extra attack happen as part of the Attack action itself, instead of needing a separate Bonus Action — effectively freeing up your Bonus Action for something else while still getting the second Light-weapon attack. Usable once per turn.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-push","title":"Push","html":"<p>Hitting a Large or smaller creature with this weapon lets you push it up to 10 feet directly away from yourself.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-sap","title":"Sap","html":"<p>Hitting a creature with this weapon gives it Disadvantage on its next attack roll, provided that attack happens before the start of your next turn.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-slow","title":"Slow","html":"<p>Hitting and damaging a creature with this weapon reduces its Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. Being hit more than once by weapons with this property in the same window doesn't reduce Speed by more than 10 feet total.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-topple","title":"Topple","html":"<p>Hitting a creature with this weapon forces a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + the ability modifier used for the attack roll + your Proficiency Bonus). On a failed save, the creature gains the Prone condition.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastery-vex","title":"Vex","html":"<p>Hitting and damaging a creature with this weapon gives you Advantage on your next attack roll against that same creature, provided that attack happens before the end of your next turn.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-weapons-simple-melee","title":"Simple Melee Weapons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-club","title":"Club","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>A crude length of wood — the default weapon of peasants, prisoners, and anyone who grabbed the nearest heavy stick.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-dagger","title":"Dagger","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-nick\">Nick</a></p><p>Small, easily concealed, and just as effective thrown as stabbed — a favorite of rogues and duelists who fight with a blade in each hand.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-greatclub","title":"Greatclub","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 2 SP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-push\">Push</a></p><p>A massive branch or timber swung with both hands — more brute force than craftsmanship.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-handaxe","title":"Handaxe","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A one-handed axe balanced well enough to throw accurately, popular with berserkers who like to open a fight at range.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-javelin","title":"Javelin","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 30/120)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>A light throwing spear; cheap enough that most militias and hunting parties carry several.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-light-hammer","title":"Light Hammer","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-nick\">Nick</a></p><p>A small, balanced hammer meant as much for throwing as for hand-to-hand work.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mace","title":"Mace","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> &mdash;</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>A simple flanged or spiked club-head on a shaft — one of the oldest weapon designs still in common use.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-quarterstaff","title":"Quarterstaff","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 2 SP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d8)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-topple\">Topple</a></p><p>A plain wooden staff, equally at home as a hiking aid, a monk's training weapon, or a traveler's only defense.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sickle","title":"Sickle","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-nick\">Nick</a></p><p>A curved farming blade repurposed as a weapon — favored in some druidic and hedge-witch traditions for its rustic symbolism.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-spear","title":"Spear","html":"<p><strong>Simple Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d8)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>Cheap, versatile, and effective thrown or thrust two-handed — the standard weapon of levied soldiers throughout most fantasy settings.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-weapons-simple-ranged","title":"Simple Ranged Weapons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-dart","title":"Dart","html":"<p><strong>Simple Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 CP &middot; Weight 1/4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A small weighted throwing spike, light enough to carry a dozen without noticing the weight.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-light-crossbow","title":"Light Crossbow","html":"<p><strong>Simple Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 80/320; Bolt), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>Requires no real strength to use effectively, which made it the weapon of choice for city watches and militia archers with minimal training.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-shortbow","title":"Shortbow","html":"<p><strong>Simple Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 80/320; Arrow), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>Compact enough to use on horseback or in tight terrain, at the cost of the longbow's range and punch.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sling","title":"Sling","html":"<p><strong>Simple Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 30/120; Bullet)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>A strip of leather or cloth used to hurl a stone or lead bullet — cheap, ancient, and still lethal in a practiced hand.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-weapons-martial-melee","title":"Martial Melee Weapons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-battleaxe","title":"Battleaxe","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d10)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-topple\">Topple</a></p><p>A single- or double-bladed axe purpose-built for combat rather than woodcutting.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-flail","title":"Flail","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> &mdash;</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>A weighted head connected to its handle by a chain, making its swing hard to predict or parry cleanly.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-glaive","title":"Glaive","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 20 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-reach\">Reach</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-graze\">Graze</a></p><p>A single-edged blade mounted on a long pole, built to keep enemies at a distance.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-greataxe","title":"Greataxe","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 7 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-cleave\">Cleave</a></p><p>A massive two-handed axe favored by barbarians and other warriors who value raw single-target damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-greatsword","title":"Greatsword","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 2d6 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-graze\">Graze</a></p><p>An enormous double-edged blade requiring both hands and real strength to wield, but capable of devastating damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-halberd","title":"Halberd","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 20 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-reach\">Reach</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-cleave\">Cleave</a></p><p>An axe blade, spike, and hook combined atop a long pole — a versatile infantry weapon good against both foot soldiers and cavalry.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lance","title":"Lance","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-reach\">Reach</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a> (unless mounted)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-topple\">Topple</a></p><p>Built for a mounted charge — unwieldy on foot (it needs both hands unless you're mounted, and it's clumsy at close range), but devastating driven home at a gallop.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> Reach, Special (you have Disadvantage when you attack a target within 5 feet of you with a lance; it requires two hands to wield unless you are mounted)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-longsword","title":"Longsword","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d10)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>The classic knightly blade — long, double-edged, and balanced for use with one hand or two.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-maul","title":"Maul","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 2d6 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-topple\">Topple</a></p><p>An oversized war hammer, more sledgehammer than tool, meant to crush through armor by sheer force.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-morningstar","title":"Morningstar","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> &mdash;</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>A spiked ball fixed atop a haft — visually similar to a flail, but rigid rather than chained, making it more predictable to swing.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pike","title":"Pike","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 18 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-reach\">Reach</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-push\">Push</a></p><p>An extremely long spear meant to be wielded in tight ranks, keeping enemy cavalry and infantry alike at a distance.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-rapier","title":"Rapier","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A slender, sharply pointed blade built for precise thrusts rather than heavy swings — the signature weapon of duelists and swashbucklers.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-scimitar","title":"Scimitar","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-nick\">Nick</a></p><p>A curved, single-edged blade favored by raiders and desert cultures, light enough to pair with a second weapon.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-shortsword","title":"Shortsword","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A short, double-edged blade — quick, easy to conceal, and a common off-hand choice for two-weapon fighters.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-trident","title":"Trident","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-thrown\">Thrown</a> (Range 20/60), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d10)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-topple\">Topple</a></p><p>A three-pronged spear traditionally associated with fishers and sea-going cultures, equally effective thrown or thrust.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing (1d8 Piercing if used with two hands)</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> Thrown (Range 20/60), Versatile</p>"},{"id":"equipment-warhammer","title":"Warhammer","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d10)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-push\">Push</a></p><p>A weighted hammerhead on a haft, built to dent armor and crush bone rather than cut.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-war-pick","title":"War Pick","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-versatile\">Versatile</a> (1d10)</p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-sap\">Sap</a></p><p>A hooked, spiked head designed to punch through armor plates that would turn aside a bladed weapon.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> &mdash;</p>"},{"id":"equipment-whip","title":"Whip","html":"<p><strong>Martial Melee Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d4 Slashing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-finesse\">Finesse</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-reach\">Reach</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>An unusual reach weapon for a light blade — trades raw damage for the ability to strike from 10 feet away without needing a polearm's bulk.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-weapons-martial-ranged","title":"Martial Ranged Weapons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-blowgun","title":"Blowgun","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 25/100; Needle), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A slender tube that fires small needles by breath alone — nearly silent, though it deals very little damage on its own.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-hand-crossbow","title":"Hand Crossbow","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 75 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d6 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 30/120; Bolt), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>Compact enough to fire one-handed, making it a natural pairing with a second weapon for characters who dabble in ranged attacks.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-heavy-crossbow","title":"Heavy Crossbow","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 18 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 100/400; Bolt), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-push\">Push</a></p><p>A large, powerful crossbow with real stopping power, at the cost of a slow reload.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-longbow","title":"Longbow","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 150/600; Arrow), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-heavy\">Heavy</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>A tall bow with exceptional range, traditionally requiring years of practice to draw and aim well.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-musket","title":"Musket","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 40/120; Bullet), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-two-handed\">Two-Handed</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-slow\">Slow</a></p><p>An early firearm — devastating on a hit, but slow enough to reload that most wielders carry a backup weapon for follow-up attacks.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon &mdash; Dungeon Master's Guide optional Firearm (Renaissance)</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> Ammunition (Range 40/120; Bullet), Loading, Two-Handed</p><p>Not part of the core Player's Handbook weapons table &mdash; available only if the DM allows the Dungeon Master's Guide's optional firearms rules.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pistol","title":"Pistol","html":"<p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-ammunition\">Ammunition</a> (Range 30/90; Bullet), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-property-loading\">Loading</a></p><p><strong>Mastery:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-mastery-vex\">Vex</a></p><p>A one-handed firearm, prized for the same reason a hand crossbow is: it frees your other hand for a second weapon or a shield.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Martial Ranged Weapon &mdash; Dungeon Master's Guide optional Firearm (Renaissance)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 Piercing</p><p><strong>Properties:</strong> Ammunition (Range 30/90; Bullet), Loading</p><p>Not part of the core Player's Handbook weapons table &mdash; available only if the DM allows the Dungeon Master's Guide's optional firearms rules.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"equipment-armor","title":"Armor","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-armor-strength-requirement","title":"Strength Requirements for Armor","html":"<p>Some armor lists a minimum Strength score. If your Strength score doesn’t meet that minimum, your Speed is reduced by 10 feet while you’re wearing it &mdash; a single flat penalty regardless of how far below the requirement your score is, identical in both editions.</p><p>This is separate from <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-training\">Armor Training</a>, which covers the (also separate, and stackable) penalty for wearing armor you lack proficiency with.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-padded-armor","title":"Padded Armor","html":"<p><strong>Light Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 8 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 11 + Dex modifier</p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 1 minute / 1 minute</p><p>Cloth or leather reinforced with layers of batting &mdash; cheap, but bulky enough that it snags and rustles.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-leather-armor","title":"Leather Armor","html":"<p><strong>Light Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 11 + Dex modifier</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 1 minute / 1 minute</p><p>The standard light armor: a stiff leather shell over a softer backing, flexible enough not to slow the wearer down.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-studded-leather-armor","title":"Studded Leather Armor","html":"<p><strong>Light Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 45 GP &middot; Weight 13 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 12 + Dex modifier</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 1 minute / 1 minute</p><p>Leather reinforced with rows of metal rivets at key points, trading a little flexibility for real protection.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-hide-armor","title":"Hide Armor","html":"<p><strong>Medium Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 12 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 12 + Dex modifier (max 2)</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 5 minutes / 1 minute</p><p>Thick furs and pelts lashed together &mdash; crude but effective, and common among tribal warriors and druids alike.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-chain-shirt-armor","title":"Chain Shirt Armor","html":"<p><strong>Medium Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 20 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 13 + Dex modifier (max 2)</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 5 minutes / 1 minute</p><p>A shirt of interlocking metal rings worn over a padded layer &mdash; popular with characters who want real protection without training in heavier armor.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-scale-mail-armor","title":"Scale Mail Armor","html":"<p><strong>Medium Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 45 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 14 + Dex modifier (max 2)</p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 5 minutes / 1 minute</p><p>Overlapping metal scales sewn onto a leather backing &mdash; good coverage, but the scales rattle and catch, making stealth harder.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-breastplate-armor","title":"Breastplate Armor","html":"<p><strong>Medium Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP &middot; Weight 20 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 14 + Dex modifier (max 2)</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 5 minutes / 1 minute</p><p>A fitted metal chestplate worn over a leather backing &mdash; solid protection without sacrificing much mobility, at a steep price.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-half-plate-armor","title":"Half Plate Armor","html":"<p><strong>Medium Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 750 GP &middot; Weight 40 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 + Dex modifier (max 2)</p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 5 minutes / 1 minute</p><p>Shaped metal plates covering most of the body, with the weaker joints left to a leather backing &mdash; excellent protection, but bulky enough to give away your position.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ring-mail-armor","title":"Ring Mail Armor","html":"<p><strong>Heavy Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 40 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 14</p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 10 minutes / 5 minutes</p><p>Leather armor studded with heavy metal rings sewn directly onto the fabric &mdash; less effective, and less common, than true chain mail.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-chain-mail-armor","title":"Chain Mail Armor","html":"<p><strong>Heavy Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 75 GP &middot; Weight 55 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 16</p><p><strong>Strength requirement:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-armor-strength-requirement\">13</a></p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 10 minutes / 5 minutes</p><p>A full coat and leggings of interlocking metal rings worn over a padded layer &mdash; heavy enough to demand real physical strength to wear well.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-splint-armor","title":"Splint Armor","html":"<p><strong>Heavy Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP &middot; Weight 60 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 17</p><p><strong>Strength requirement:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-armor-strength-requirement\">15</a></p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 10 minutes / 5 minutes</p><p>Vertical strips of metal riveted to a leather backing &mdash; a demanding but well-protected suit favored by front-line warriors.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-plate-armor","title":"Plate Armor","html":"<p><strong>Heavy Armor</strong> &middot; Cost 1,500 GP &middot; Weight 65 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 18</p><p><strong>Strength requirement:</strong> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-armor-strength-requirement\">15</a></p><p><strong>Stealth:</strong> Disadvantage</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 10 minutes / 5 minutes</p><p>A full suit of shaped and fitted metal plates covering the entire body &mdash; the pinnacle of mundane protection, and priced accordingly.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-shield","title":"Shield","html":"<p><strong>Shield</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> +2 while equipped</p><p><strong>Don/Doff:</strong> 1 action / 1 action</p><p>A broad piece of wood or metal strapped to one arm, adding significant protection at the cost of a free hand.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-tools","title":"Tools","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-tools-artisans","title":"Artisan's Tools","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-alchemist-s-supplies","title":"Alchemist's Supplies","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 8 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Identify a substance (DC 15), or start a fire (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Acid, Alchemist's Fire, Component Pouch, Oil, Paper, Perfume</p>"},{"id":"equipment-brewer-s-supplies","title":"Brewer's Supplies","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 20 GP &middot; Weight 9 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Detect poisoned drink (DC 15), or identify alcohol (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Antitoxin</p>"},{"id":"equipment-calligrapher-s-supplies","title":"Calligrapher's Supplies","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Write text with impressive flourishes that guard against forgery (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Ink, Spell Scroll</p>"},{"id":"equipment-carpenter-s-tools","title":"Carpenter's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 8 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Strength</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Seal or pry open a door or container (DC 20)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Club, Greatclub, Quarterstaff, Barrel, Chest, Ladder, Pole, Portable Ram, Torch</p>"},{"id":"equipment-cartographer-s-tools","title":"Cartographer's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Draft a map of a small area (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Map</p>"},{"id":"equipment-cobbler-s-tools","title":"Cobbler's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Modify footwear to give Advantage on the wearer's next Dexterity (Acrobatics) check (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Climber's Kit</p>"},{"id":"equipment-cook-s-utensils","title":"Cook's Utensils","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 8 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Improve food's flavor (DC 10), or detect spoiled or poisoned food (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Rations</p>"},{"id":"equipment-glassblower-s-tools","title":"Glassblower's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern what a glass object held in the past 24 hours (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Glass Bottle, Magnifying Glass, Spyglass, Vial</p>"},{"id":"equipment-jeweler-s-tools","title":"Jeweler's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern a gem's value (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Arcane Focus, Holy Symbol</p>"},{"id":"equipment-leatherworker-s-tools","title":"Leatherworker's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Add a design to a leather item (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Sling, Whip, Hide Armor, Leather Armor, Studded Leather Armor, Backpack, Crossbow Bolt Case, Map or Scroll Case, Parchment, Pouch, Quiver, Waterskin</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mason-s-tools","title":"Mason's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 8 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Strength</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Chisel a symbol or hole in stone (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Block and Tackle</p>"},{"id":"equipment-painter-s-supplies","title":"Painter's Supplies","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Paint a recognizable image of something you've seen (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Druidic Focus, Holy Symbol</p>"},{"id":"equipment-potter-s-tools","title":"Potter's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern what a ceramic object held in the past 24 hours (DC 15)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Jug, Lamp</p>"},{"id":"equipment-smith-s-tools","title":"Smith's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 20 GP &middot; Weight 8 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Strength</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Pry open a door or container (DC 20)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Any Melee weapon (except Club, Greatclub, Quarterstaff, and Whip), Medium armor (except Hide), Heavy armor, Ball Bearings, Bucket, Caltrops, Chain, Crowbar, Firearm Bullets, Grappling Hook, Iron Pot, Iron Spikes, Sling Bullets</p>"},{"id":"equipment-tinker-s-tools","title":"Tinker's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Assemble a Tiny item composed of scrap, which falls apart in 1 minute (DC 20)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Musket, Pistol, Bell, Bullseye Lantern, Flask, Hooded Lantern, Hunting Trap, Lock, Manacles, Mirror, Shovel, Signal Whistle, Tinderbox</p>"},{"id":"equipment-weaver-s-tools","title":"Weaver's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Mend a tear in clothing (DC 10), or sew a Tiny design (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Padded Armor, Basket, Bedroll, Blanket, Fine Clothes, Net, Robe, Rope, Sack, String, Tent, Traveler's Clothes</p>"},{"id":"equipment-woodcarver-s-tools","title":"Woodcarver's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Artisan's Tools</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Carve a pattern in wood (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Club, Greatclub, Quarterstaff, Ranged weapons (except Pistol, Musket, and Sling), Arcane Focus, Arrows, Bolts, Druidic Focus, Ink Pen, Needles</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-tools-gaming-sets","title":"Gaming Sets","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-dice-set","title":"Dice Set","html":"<p><strong>Gaming Set</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern whether someone is cheating (DC 10), or win the game (DC 20)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-dragonchess-set","title":"Dragonchess Set","html":"<p><strong>Gaming Set</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern whether someone is cheating (DC 10), or win the game (DC 20)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-playing-card-set","title":"Playing Card Set","html":"<p><strong>Gaming Set</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern whether someone is cheating (DC 10), or win the game (DC 20)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-three-dragon-ante-set","title":"Three-Dragon Ante Set","html":"<p><strong>Gaming Set</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Discern whether someone is cheating (DC 10), or win the game (DC 20)</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-tools-musical-instruments","title":"Musical Instruments","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-bagpipes","title":"Bagpipes","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-drum","title":"Drum","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 6 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-dulcimer","title":"Dulcimer","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-flute","title":"Flute","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-horn","title":"Horn","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 3 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lute","title":"Lute","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 35 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lyre","title":"Lyre","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pan-flute","title":"Pan Flute","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 12 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-shawm","title":"Shawm","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-viol","title":"Viol","html":"<p><strong>Musical Instrument</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Play a known tune (DC 10), or improvise a song (DC 15)</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-tools-other","title":"Other Tools","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-disguise-kit","title":"Disguise Kit","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Apply makeup (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Costume</p>"},{"id":"equipment-forgery-kit","title":"Forgery Kit","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Mimic 10 or fewer words of someone else's handwriting (DC 15), or duplicate a wax seal (DC 20)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-herbalism-kit","title":"Herbalism Kit","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Identify a plant (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Antitoxin, Candle, Healer's Kit, Potion of Healing</p>"},{"id":"equipment-navigator-s-tools","title":"Navigator's Tools","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Wisdom</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Plot a course (DC 10), or determine position by stargazing (DC 15)</p>"},{"id":"equipment-poisoner-s-kit","title":"Poisoner's Kit","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Intelligence</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Detect a poisoned object (DC 10)</p><p><strong>Craft:</strong> Basic Poison</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p>Doesn’t appear in the core 2014 Player’s Handbook tool list at all &mdash; it comes from Xanathar’s Guide to Everything, with the same cost and weight.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-thieves-tools","title":"Thieves' Tools","html":"<p><strong>Tool</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p><strong>Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><strong>Utilize:</strong> Pick a lock (DC 15), or disarm a trap (DC 15)</p>"}]}]},{"id":"equipment-adventuring-gear","title":"Adventuring Gear","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-acid","title":"Acid","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>As part of the Attack action, you can throw this vial up to 20 feet at a creature or object you can see, shattering it on impact. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your Dexterity modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or take 2d6 Acid damage.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>As an action, you can splash the contents of this vial onto a creature within 5 feet of you, or throw it up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. In either case, make a ranged attack roll against a creature or object, treating the acid as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 Acid damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-alchemist-s-fire","title":"Alchemist's Fire","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>As part of the Attack action, you can throw this flask up to 20 feet at a creature or object you can see, shattering it on impact. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your Dexterity modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or take 1d4 Fire damage and catch fire, taking the Burning condition's ongoing damage.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>This sticky, flammable substance ignites when exposed to air. As an action, you can throw this flask up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. Make a ranged attack roll against a creature or object, treating the flask as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns. A creature can end this damage by using its action to make a DC 10 Dexterity check to extinguish the flames.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-antitoxin","title":"Antitoxin","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can drink a vial of Antitoxin to gain Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition for 1 hour.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>You gain Advantage on saving throws against poison for 1 hour after drinking this vial. It confers no benefit to undead or constructs.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-backpack","title":"Backpack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>A Backpack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot. It can also serve as a saddlebag.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ball-bearings","title":"Ball Bearings","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can spill Ball Bearings from their pouch to cover a level, 10-foot-square area within 10 feet of yourself. A creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or gain the Prone condition. It takes 10 minutes to recover the Ball Bearings afterward.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>As an action, you can spill these tiny metal balls from their pouch to cover a level, 10-foot-square area. Each creature that moves across the area must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or fall prone. A creature moving through the area at half speed doesn't need to make the save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-barrel","title":"Barrel","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 70 lb.</p><p>A Barrel holds up to 40 gallons of liquid or up to 4 cubic feet of dry goods.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-basket","title":"Basket","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 4 SP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Basket holds up to 40 pounds within 2 cubic feet.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-bedroll","title":"Bedroll","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 7 lb.</p><p>A Bedroll sleeps one Small or Medium creature. While in a Bedroll, you automatically succeed on saving throws against extreme cold.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-bell","title":"Bell","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>When rung as a Utilize action, a Bell produces a sound that can be heard up to 60 feet away.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-blanket","title":"Blanket","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p>While wrapped in a Blanket, you have Advantage on saving throws against extreme cold.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-block-and-tackle","title":"Block and Tackle","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>A Block and Tackle allows you to hoist up to four times the weight you can normally lift.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-book","title":"Book","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>A Book contains fiction or nonfiction. If you consult an accurate nonfiction Book about its topic, you gain a +5 bonus to Intelligence (Arcana, History, Nature, or Religion) checks you make about that topic.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-bottle-glass","title":"Bottle, Glass","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Glass Bottle holds up to 1&#189; pints.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-bucket","title":"Bucket","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 CP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Bucket holds up to half a cubic foot of contents.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-caltrops","title":"Caltrops","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can spread Caltrops from their bag to cover a 5-foot-square area within 5 feet of yourself. A creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 1 Piercing damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. It takes 10 minutes to recover the Caltrops afterward.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>As an action, you can spread these sharp spikes from their bag to cover a 5-foot-square area. Each creature that enters the area must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or stop moving this turn and take 1 Piercing damage. Taking this damage reduces the creature's walking Speed by 10 feet until it regains at least 1 hit point. A creature moving through the area at half speed doesn't need to make the save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-candle","title":"Candle","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 CP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>For 1 hour, a lit Candle sheds Bright Light in a 5-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 5 feet.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-case-crossbow-bolt","title":"Case, Crossbow Bolt","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Crossbow Bolt Case holds up to 20 Bolts.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-case-map-or-scroll","title":"Case, Map or Scroll","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Map or Scroll Case holds up to 10 sheets of paper or 5 sheets of parchment.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-chain","title":"Chain","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can wrap a Chain around an unwilling creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition, provided you succeed on a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check. If the creature's legs are bound, it has the Restrained condition until it escapes. Escaping requires a successful DC 18 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check as an action; bursting the Chain requires a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check as an action.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p>A Chain has 10 hit points. It can be burst with a successful DC 20 Strength check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-chest","title":"Chest","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 25 lb.</p><p>A Chest holds up to 12 cubic feet of contents.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-climber-s-kit","title":"Climber's Kit","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 12 lb.</p><p>A Climber's Kit includes boot tips, gloves, pitons, and a harness. As a Utilize action, you can use the kit to anchor yourself; when you do, you can't fall more than 25 feet from the anchor point, and you can't move more than 25 feet from there without undoing the anchor as a Bonus Action.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-clothes-fine","title":"Clothes, Fine","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 15 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p>Fine Clothes are made of expensive fabrics and adorned with expertly crafted details. Some events and locations admit only people wearing these clothes.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-clothes-traveler-s","title":"Clothes, Traveler's","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>Traveler's Clothes are resilient garments designed for travel in various environments.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-component-pouch","title":"Component Pouch","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Component Pouch is watertight and filled with compartments that hold all the free Material components of your spells.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-costume","title":"Costume","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>While wearing a Costume, you have Advantage on any ability check you make to impersonate the person or type of person it represents.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>Called \"Clothes, Costume.\" While wearing this costume, you have Advantage on any ability check you make to impersonate a different person.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-crowbar","title":"Crowbar","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>Using a Crowbar gives you Advantage on Strength checks where the crowbar's leverage can be applied.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-flask","title":"Flask","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 CP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Flask holds up to 1 pint.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 CP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>Called \"Flask or Tankard.\" It holds up to 1 pint of liquid.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-grappling-hook","title":"Grappling Hook","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can throw the Grappling Hook at a railing, ledge, or other catch within 50 feet of yourself; the hook catches if you succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. If you've tied a Rope to it, you can then climb the rope.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>A Grappling Hook can be attached to a Rope and thrown, dropped, or lowered to catch on an available surface or object. It has no formal mechanic of its own; the DM determines whether and how it catches.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-healer-s-kit","title":"Healer's Kit","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p>A Healer's Kit has ten uses. As a Utilize action, you can expend one of its uses to stabilize an Unconscious creature at 0 Hit Points without needing to make a Wisdom (Medicine) check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-holy-water","title":"Holy Water","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>As part of the Attack action, you can throw this flask up to 20 feet at a creature you can see, shattering it on impact. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your Dexterity modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or take 2d8 Radiant damage if it is a Fiend or an Undead.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>As an action, you can splash the contents of this flask onto a creature within 5 feet of you, or throw it up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. Make a ranged attack roll against a target creature, treating the holy water as an improvised weapon. A Fiend or Undead hit by it takes 2d6 Radiant damage. A cleric or paladin can create Holy Water by performing a special ritual that takes 1 hour and uses 25 GP of powdered silver; the ritual consumes the silver and expends a 1st-level spell slot.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-hunting-trap","title":"Hunting Trap","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 25 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can set a Hunting Trap, a sawtooth steel ring that snaps shut when a creature steps on a pressure plate in the center. It's affixed by a heavy chain to an immobile object, such as a tree or a spike driven into the ground. A creature that steps on the plate must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 1d4 Piercing damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn; thereafter, until it breaks free, its movement is limited by the chain's length (typically 3 feet). A creature can use its action to make a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing itself or another creature within reach on a success; each failed check deals 1 Piercing damage to the trapped creature.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ink","title":"Ink","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>Ink comes in a 1-ounce bottle, enough to write about 500 pages.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ink-pen","title":"Ink Pen","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 CP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>Using Ink, an Ink Pen is used to write or draw.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-jug","title":"Jug","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 CP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>A Jug holds up to 1 gallon.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 CP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>Called \"Jug or Pitcher.\" It holds up to 1 gallon of liquid.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ladder","title":"Ladder","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight 25 lb.</p><p>A Ladder is 10 feet tall. You must climb to move up or down it.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lamp","title":"Lamp","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Lamp burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 15-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lantern-bullseye","title":"Lantern, Bullseye","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Bullseye Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 60-foot cone and Dim Light for an additional 60 feet.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lantern-hooded","title":"Lantern, Hooded","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Hooded Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. As a Bonus Action, you can lower the hood (reducing the light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius) or raise it again.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Hooded Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. As an action, you can lower the hood to reduce the light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius, or raise it again.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lock","title":"Lock","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Lock comes with a key. Without the key, a creature can use Thieves' Tools to pick this Lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-magnifying-glass","title":"Magnifying Glass","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 100 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>A Magnifying Glass grants Advantage on any ability check made to appraise or inspect a highly detailed item. Lighting a fire with one requires light as bright as sunlight to focus, tinder to ignite, and about 5 minutes for the fire to catch.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-manacles","title":"Manacles","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can use Manacles to bind an unwilling Small or Medium creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition, provided you succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check. While bound, a creature has Disadvantage on attack rolls, and is Restrained if the Manacles are attached to a fixed chain or hook. Escaping requires a successful DC 20 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check as an action; bursting them requires a successful DC 25 Strength (Athletics) check as an action. Each set comes with a key; without it, a creature can use Thieves' Tools to pick the lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 6 lb.</p><p>Manacles have 15 hit points. They can bind a Small or Medium creature. Escaping requires a DC 20 Dexterity check; bursting them requires a DC 20 Strength check. Each set comes with one key. Without the key, a creature proficient with Thieves' Tools can pick the lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-map","title":"Map","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>If you consult an accurate Map, you gain a +5 bonus to Wisdom (Survival) checks you make to find your way in the place it represents.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mirror","title":"Mirror","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight &#189; lb.</p><p>A handheld steel Mirror is useful for personal cosmetics, but also for peeking around corners and reflecting light as a signal.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight &#189; lb.</p><p>Called \"Mirror, Steel.\" This handheld steel mirror is useful for personal cosmetics, but also for peeking around corners and reflecting light as a signal.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-net","title":"Net","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p>As part of the Attack action, you can throw a Net at a creature you can see within 15 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your Dexterity modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or gain the Restrained condition until it escapes (automatically succeeding if it's Huge or larger). To escape, the target or a creature within 5 feet of it must take an action and succeed on a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing the Restrained creature on a success. Destroying the Net (AC 10, 5 HP, Immunity to Bludgeoning, Poison, and Psychic damage) also frees the target.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p>The Net is a Martial Ranged weapon rather than Adventuring Gear (Thrown, Range 5/15). As an action, you can make a ranged attack roll against a Large or smaller creature. On a hit, the target has the Restrained condition until it's freed; the net has no effect on a formless creature or a creature that is Huge or larger. A creature can use its action to make a DC 10 Strength check, freeing itself or another creature within its reach from the net on a success. Dealing 5 Slashing damage to the net (AC 10) also frees the creature without harming it, and destroys the net. A net attack can only ever be made once, regardless of how many attacks you're normally entitled to.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-oil","title":"Oil","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>You can douse a creature, object, or space with Oil, or use it as fuel. <strong>Dousing a creature or object:</strong> as part of the Attack action, throw the flask at a target within 20 feet; it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 + your Dexterity modifier + Proficiency Bonus) or be covered in oil, taking an extra 5 Fire damage if it takes any Fire damage before the oil dries (after 1 minute). <strong>Dousing a space:</strong> as a Utilize action, pour the flask on level ground to cover a 5-foot-square area within 5 feet of yourself; if lit, the oil burns until the end of the turn 2 rounds later, dealing 5 Fire damage (once per turn) to any creature that enters the area or ends its turn there. <strong>Fuel:</strong> a flask burns for 6 hours (not necessarily consecutively) in a Lamp or Lantern.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>You can splash the contents of this flask onto a creature within 5 feet of you, or throw it up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact, as an action. Make a ranged attack roll against the target, treating the oil as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target is covered in oil; if it takes any Fire damage before the oil dries (after 1 minute), it takes an extra 5 Fire damage. A flask of oil can also fuel a Lamp or Lantern for 6 hours.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-paper","title":"Paper","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>One sheet of Paper can hold about 250 handwritten words.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-parchment","title":"Parchment","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>One sheet of Parchment can hold about 250 handwritten words.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-perfume","title":"Perfume","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>Perfume comes in a 4-ounce vial. For 1 hour after applying it, you have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to influence an Indifferent Humanoid within 5 feet of yourself.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-poison-basic","title":"Poison, Basic","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 100 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can use a vial of Basic Poison to coat one weapon or up to three pieces of ammunition. A creature that takes Piercing or Slashing damage from the poisoned weapon or ammunition takes an extra 1d4 Poison damage. Once applied, the poison retains potency for 1 minute or until its damage is dealt, whichever comes first.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 100 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>As an action, you can use a vial of this poison to coat one slashing or piercing weapon, or up to three pieces of ammunition. A creature hit by the poisoned weapon or ammunition must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or take 1d4 Poison damage. Once applied, the poison retains potency for 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pole","title":"Pole","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 CP &middot; Weight 7 lb.</p><p>A Pole is 10 feet long. You can use it to touch something up to 10 feet away. If you must make a Strength (Athletics) check as part of a High or Long Jump, you can use the Pole to vault, giving yourself Advantage on the check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pot-iron","title":"Pot, Iron","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb.</p><p>An Iron Pot holds up to 1 gallon.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pouch","title":"Pouch","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Pouch holds up to 6 pounds within one-fifth of a cubic foot.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-quiver","title":"Quiver","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Quiver holds up to 20 Arrows.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-ram-portable","title":"Ram, Portable","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 4 GP &middot; Weight 35 lb.</p><p>You can use a Portable Ram to break down doors, gaining a +4 bonus to the Strength check. One other character can help you use it, giving you Advantage on the check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-rations","title":"Rations","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>Rations consist of travel-ready food, including jerky, dried fruit, hardtack, and nuts. See Malnutrition for the risks of not eating enough.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-robe","title":"Robe","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>A Robe has vocational or ceremonial significance. Some events and locations admit only people wearing a Robe of certain colors or symbols.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>Called \"Robes.\" A robe has vocational or ceremonial significance to the wearer.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-rope","title":"Rope","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>As a Utilize action, you can tie a knot with Rope if you succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check; it can be burst with a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check. You can bind an unwilling creature with it only if the creature has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition; if its legs are bound this way, it has the Restrained condition until it escapes, which requires a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check as an action.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 10 lb. per 50 ft. (Hempen); 5 lb. per 50 ft. (Silk, 10 GP)</p><p>Rope, whether made of hemp or silk, has 2 hit points and can be burst with a successful DC 17 Strength check.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sack","title":"Sack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 CP &middot; Weight &#189; lb.</p><p>A Sack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-shovel","title":"Shovel","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>Working for 1 hour, you can use a Shovel to dig a hole 5 feet on each side in soil or similar material.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-signal-whistle","title":"Signal Whistle","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 CP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>When blown as a Utilize action, a Signal Whistle produces a sound that can be heard up to 600 feet away.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-spikes-iron","title":"Spikes, Iron","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 5 lb.</p><p>Iron Spikes come in bundles of ten. As a Utilize action, you can use a blunt object (such as a Light Hammer) to hammer a spike into wood, earth, or similar material &mdash; to jam a door shut, or to then tie a Rope or Chain to it.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-spyglass","title":"Spyglass","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1,000 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>Objects viewed through a Spyglass are magnified to twice their size.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-string","title":"String","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 SP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>String is 10 feet long. You can tie a knot in it as a Utilize action.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-tent","title":"Tent","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 20 lb.</p><p>A Tent sleeps up to two Small or Medium creatures.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 GP &middot; Weight 20 lb.</p><p>Called \"Tent, Two-Person.\" It sleeps up to two Small or Medium creatures.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-tinderbox","title":"Tinderbox","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Tinderbox holds flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil), used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a Candle, Lamp, Lantern, Torch, or anything else with exposed fuel takes a Bonus Action; lighting any other fire takes 1 minute.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 5 SP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Tinderbox holds flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil), used to kindle a fire. Lighting a Candle, Lamp, Lantern, Torch, or anything else with exposed fuel takes an action. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-torch","title":"Torch","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 CP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Torch burns for 1 hour, casting Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet. As part of the Attack action, you can attack with it as a Simple Melee weapon; on a hit, the target takes 1 Fire damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-vial","title":"Vial","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>A Vial holds up to 4 ounces.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-waterskin","title":"Waterskin","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 2 SP &middot; Weight 5 lb. (full)</p><p>A Waterskin holds up to 4 pints. If you don't drink sufficient water, you risk dehydration.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-ammunition","title":"Ammunition","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-arrows","title":"Arrows","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A quiver of 20 Arrows, used by Shortbows and Longbows. Required by a weapon with the Ammunition property; a weapon's own entry specifies which type it uses. Recovering half the ammunition used (round down) after a fight takes 1 minute of searching; the rest is lost.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-bolts","title":"Bolts","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1&#189; lb.</p><p>A case of 20 Bolts, used by Light, Hand, and Heavy Crossbows. Required by a weapon with the Ammunition property; a weapon's own entry specifies which type it uses. Recovering half the ammunition used (round down) after a fight takes 1 minute of searching; the rest is lost.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1&#189; lb.</p><p>Called \"Crossbow Bolts.\" A case holds 20 bolts, used by Light, Hand, and Heavy Crossbows.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-firearm-bullets","title":"Firearm Bullets","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 3 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A pouch of 10 Firearm Bullets, used by the Musket and Pistol. Required by a weapon with the Ammunition property; a weapon's own entry specifies which type it uses. Recovering half the ammunition used (round down) after a fight takes 1 minute of searching; the rest is lost.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 3 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>Firearm Bullets exist only alongside the Dungeon Master's Guide's optional Musket and Pistol rules; a pouch holds 10 bullets.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sling-bullets","title":"Sling Bullets","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 4 CP &middot; Weight 1&#189; lb.</p><p>A pouch of 20 Sling Bullets, used by the Sling. Required by a weapon with the Ammunition property; a weapon's own entry specifies which type it uses. Recovering half the ammunition used (round down) after a fight takes 1 minute of searching; the rest is lost.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 4 CP &middot; Weight 1&#189; lb.</p><p>Called \"Bullets, Sling.\" A pouch holds 20 bullets, used by the Sling.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-needles","title":"Needles","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A pouch of 50 Needles, used by the Blowgun. Required by a weapon with the Ammunition property; a weapon's own entry specifies which type it uses. Recovering half the ammunition used (round down) after a fight takes 1 minute of searching; the rest is lost.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>Called \"Blowgun Needles.\" A pouch holds 50 needles, used by the Blowgun.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-spellcasting-foci","title":"Spellcasting Foci & Holy Symbols","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-arcane-foci","title":"Arcane Foci","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-crystal","title":"Crystal","html":"<p><strong>Arcane Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>An Arcane Focus, usable by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-orb","title":"Orb","html":"<p><strong>Arcane Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 20 GP &middot; Weight 3 lb.</p><p>An Arcane Focus, usable by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-rod-focus","title":"Rod (Focus)","html":"<p><strong>Arcane Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>An Arcane Focus, usable by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-staff-focus","title":"Staff (Focus)","html":"<p><strong>Arcane Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>An Arcane Focus (also usable as a Quarterstaff), usable by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-wand-focus","title":"Wand (Focus)","html":"<p><strong>Arcane Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>An Arcane Focus, usable by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-druidic-foci","title":"Druidic Foci","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-sprig-of-mistletoe","title":"Sprig of Mistletoe","html":"<p><strong>Druidic Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 1 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>A Druidic Focus, usable by a Druid or Ranger as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-wooden-staff-focus","title":"Wooden Staff (Focus)","html":"<p><strong>Druidic Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 4 lb.</p><p>A Druidic Focus (also usable as a Quarterstaff), usable by a Druid or Ranger as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-yew-wand","title":"Yew Wand","html":"<p><strong>Druidic Focus</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Druidic Focus, usable by a Druid or Ranger as a Spellcasting Focus.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Yew Wand is a Druidic Focus, usable by a Druid as a Spellcasting Focus. A Totem (1 GP, no listed weight) is also available as a Druidic Focus.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-holy-symbols","title":"Holy Symbols","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-amulet","title":"Amulet","html":"<p><strong>Holy Symbol</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 1 lb.</p><p>A Holy Symbol, worn or held. Usable by a Cleric or Paladin as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-emblem","title":"Emblem","html":"<p><strong>Holy Symbol</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight &mdash;</p><p>A Holy Symbol, borne on fabric (such as a tabard or banner) or a Shield. Usable by a Cleric or Paladin as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-reliquary","title":"Reliquary","html":"<p><strong>Holy Symbol</strong> &middot; Cost 5 GP &middot; Weight 2 lb.</p><p>A Holy Symbol, held. Usable by a Cleric or Paladin as a Spellcasting Focus.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"equipment-packs","title":"Equipment Packs","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-burglar-s-pack","title":"Burglar's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 16 GP &middot; Weight 42 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Ball Bearings, Bell, 10 Candles, Crowbar, Hooded Lantern, 7 flasks of Oil, 5 days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, and a Waterskin.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 16 GP &middot; Weight 44&#189; lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, a bag of 1,000 Ball Bearings, 10 feet of String, Bell, 5 Candles, Crowbar, Hammer, 10 Pitons, Hooded Lantern, 2 flasks of Oil, 5 days of Rations, Tinderbox, and a Waterskin, plus 50 feet of Hempen Rope strapped to the outside.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-diplomat-s-pack","title":"Diplomat's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 39 GP &middot; Weight 39 lb.</p><p>Contains: Chest, Fine Clothes, Ink, 5 Ink Pens, Lamp, 2 Map or Scroll Cases, 4 flasks of Oil, 5 sheets of Paper, 5 sheets of Parchment, Perfume, and Tinderbox.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 39 GP &middot; Weight 39 lb.</p><p>Contains: Chest, 2 Map or Scroll Cases, Fine Clothes, a bottle of Ink, an Ink Pen, Lamp, 2 flasks of Oil, 5 sheets of Paper, a vial of Perfume, Sealing Wax, and Soap.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-dungeoneer-s-pack","title":"Dungeoneer's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 12 GP &middot; Weight 55 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Caltrops, Crowbar, 2 flasks of Oil, 10 days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, 10 Torches, and a Waterskin.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 12 GP &middot; Weight 61&#189; lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Crowbar, Hammer, 10 Pitons, 10 Torches, Tinderbox, 10 days of Rations, and a Waterskin, plus 50 feet of Hempen Rope strapped to the outside.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-entertainer-s-pack","title":"Entertainer's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 40 GP &middot; Weight 58&#189; lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Bedroll, Bell, Bullseye Lantern, 3 Costumes, Mirror, 8 flasks of Oil, 9 days of Rations, Tinderbox, and a Waterskin.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 40 GP &middot; Weight 38 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Bedroll, 2 Costumes, 5 Candles, 5 days of Rations, a Waterskin, and a Disguise Kit.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-explorer-s-pack","title":"Explorer's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 55 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Bedroll, 2 flasks of Oil, 10 days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, 10 Torches, and a Waterskin.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 10 GP &middot; Weight 59 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Bedroll, Mess Kit, Tinderbox, 10 Torches, 10 days of Rations, and a Waterskin, plus 50 feet of Hempen Rope strapped to the outside.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-priest-s-pack","title":"Priest's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 33 GP &middot; Weight 29 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Blanket, Holy Water, Lamp, 7 days of Rations, Robe, and Tinderbox.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 19 GP &middot; Weight 24 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Blanket, 10 Candles, Tinderbox, an Alms Box, 2 blocks of Incense, a Censer, Vestments, 2 days of Rations, and a Waterskin.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-scholar-s-pack","title":"Scholar's Pack","html":"<p><strong>Adventuring Gear</strong> &middot; Cost 40 GP &middot; Weight 22 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, Book, Ink, Ink Pen, Lamp, 10 flasks of Oil, 10 sheets of Parchment, and Tinderbox.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Equipment Pack</strong> &middot; Cost 40 GP &middot; Weight 11 lb.</p><p>Contains: Backpack, a Book of lore, a bottle of Ink, an Ink Pen, 10 sheets of Parchment, a small bag of sand, and a small knife.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-mounts","title":"Mounts","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-camel","title":"Camel","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 50 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 450 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-elephant","title":"Elephant","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 40 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 1,320 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-horse-draft","title":"Horse, Draft","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 50 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 40 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 540 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-horse-riding","title":"Horse, Riding","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 75 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 60 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 480 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mastiff","title":"Mastiff","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 25 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 40 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 195 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-mule","title":"Mule","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 8 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 40 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 420 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pony","title":"Pony","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 30 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 40 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 225 lb.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-warhorse","title":"Warhorse","html":"<p><strong>Mount</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 60 ft. &middot; <strong>Carrying Capacity:</strong> 540 lb.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-tack-harness","title":"Tack, Harness & Drawn Vehicles","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-carriage","title":"Carriage","html":"<p><strong>Drawn Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 100 GP &middot; Weight: 600 lb.</p><p>An enclosed, four-wheeled vehicle for passengers, typically pulled by a team of two or four horses. Built for comfort over rough travel, and best suited to reasonably maintained roads.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-cart","title":"Cart","html":"<p><strong>Drawn Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 15 GP &middot; Weight: 200 lb.</p><p>A simple two-wheeled cart pulled by a single draft animal, common for hauling modest loads short distances.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-chariot","title":"Chariot","html":"<p><strong>Drawn Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 250 GP &middot; Weight: 100 lb.</p><p>A light, open, two-wheeled vehicle built for speed rather than cargo, traditionally used in racing, ceremony, or war.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-feed-per-day","title":"Feed (per day)","html":"<p><strong>Tack</strong> &middot; Cost: 5 CP &middot; Weight: 10 lb.</p><p>One day's feed for one mount.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-saddle-exotic","title":"Saddle, Exotic","html":"<p><strong>Tack</strong> &middot; Cost: 60 GP &middot; Weight: 40 lb.</p><p>Required for riding an aquatic or flying mount. Comes with a bit, bridle, reins, and any other equipment needed to use it.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-saddle-military","title":"Saddle, Military","html":"<p><strong>Tack</strong> &middot; Cost: 20 GP &middot; Weight: 30 lb.</p><p>Braces the rider, giving Advantage on any ability check made to remain mounted. Comes with a bit, bridle, reins, and any other equipment needed to use it.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-saddle-riding","title":"Saddle, Riding","html":"<p><strong>Tack</strong> &middot; Cost: 10 GP &middot; Weight: 25 lb.</p><p>Comes with a bit, bridle, reins, and any other equipment needed to use it.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p>A fourth variant, the Pack Saddle (5 GP, 15 lb.), is also available alongside Exotic, Military, and Riding saddles. Two further items exist with no 2024 equivalent: Bit and Bridle (2 GP, 1 lb.), and Saddlebags (4 GP, 8 lb.), which hold gear the way a Backpack does. Saddles are listed in their own separate table rather than merged into Tack, Harness, and Drawn Vehicles.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sled","title":"Sled","html":"<p><strong>Drawn Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 20 GP &middot; Weight: 300 lb.</p><p>A vehicle fitted with runners instead of wheels, built for hauling loads across snow or ice.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-stabling-per-day","title":"Stabling (per day)","html":"<p><strong>Tack</strong> &middot; Cost: 5 SP &middot; Weight: &mdash;</p><p>One day of stabling, feed, and water for one mount.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-wagon","title":"Wagon","html":"<p><strong>Drawn Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 35 GP &middot; Weight: 400 lb.</p><p>A sturdy four-wheeled vehicle for hauling heavy cargo, typically pulled by a team of two or more draft animals.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-barding","title":"Barding","html":"<p>Barding is armor made for a mount, protecting its head, neck, chest, and body. Any armor on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"equipment-armor\">Armor table</a> can be bought as barding: it costs four times the normal price and weighs twice as much as the equivalent armor made for a Small or Medium humanoid.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-vehicles-waterborne","title":"Airborne & Waterborne Vehicles","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-airship","title":"Airship","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 40,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 8 mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 10 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 20 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> 1 ton</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 13 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 300 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> &mdash;</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p>Doesn't exist &mdash; the Airship is a 2024-only addition.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-galley","title":"Galley","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 30,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 4 mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 80 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> &mdash; &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> 150 tons</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 500 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> 20</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 30,000 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 4 mph</p>"},{"id":"equipment-keelboat","title":"Keelboat","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 3,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 1 mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 1 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 6 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> &#189; ton</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 100 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> 10</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 3,000 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 1 mph</p>"},{"id":"equipment-longship","title":"Longship","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 10,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 3 mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 40 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 150 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> 10 tons</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 300 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> 15</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 10,000 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 3 mph</p>"},{"id":"equipment-rowboat","title":"Rowboat","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 50 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 1&#189; mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 1 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 3 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> &mdash;</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 11 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 50 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> &mdash;</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 50 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 1&#189; mph</p>"},{"id":"equipment-sailing-ship","title":"Sailing Ship","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 10,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 2 mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 20 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 20 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> 100 tons</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 300 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> 15</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 10,000 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 2 mph</p>"},{"id":"equipment-warship","title":"Warship","html":"<p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 25,000 GP</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 2&#189; mph &middot; <strong>Crew:</strong> 60 &middot; <strong>Passengers:</strong> 60 &middot; <strong>Cargo:</strong> 200 tons</p><p><strong>AC:</strong> 15 &middot; <strong>HP:</strong> 500 &middot; <strong>Damage Threshold:</strong> 20</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Vehicle</strong> &middot; Cost: 25,000 GP<br><strong>Speed:</strong> 2&#189; mph</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-poisons","title":"Poisons","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-assassin-s-blood","title":"Assassin's Blood","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 6 (1d12) Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't Poisoned.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-burnt-othur-fumes","title":"Burnt Othur Fumes","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, then repeat the saving throw at the start of each of its turns, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each further failure. The poison ends after three successful saves.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-carrion-crawler-mucus","title":"Carrion Crawler Mucus","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated carrion crawler. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Paralyzed conditions for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect early.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Crawler Mucus.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-essence-of-ether","title":"Essence of Ether","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 300 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 8 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lolth-s-sting","title":"Lolth's Sting","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Drow Poison.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also falls Unconscious for the same duration. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-malice","title":"Malice","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Blinded conditions for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-midnight-tears","title":"Midnight Tears","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature that ingests this poison suffers no effect until the stroke of midnight. If the poison hasn't been neutralized by then, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or take 9d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-oil-of-taggit","title":"Oil of Taggit","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pale-tincture","title":"Pale Tincture","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition. The Poisoned creature repeats the save every 24 hours, taking another 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each failure; none of this damage can be healed by any means while the creature remains Poisoned. After seven successful saves, the creature is no longer Poisoned and can heal normally.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-purple-worm-poison","title":"Purple Worm Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 21 Constitution saving throw or take 10d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution saving throw or take 12d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-serpent-venom","title":"Serpent Venom","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated giant poisonous snake. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 3d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-torpor","title":"Torpor","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and have its Speed halved for 4d6 hours.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 4d6 hours.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-truth-serum","title":"Truth Serum","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and be unable to speak a deliberate lie for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-wyvern-poison","title":"Wyvern Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 7d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}]},{"id":"equipment-trade-goods","title":"Trade Goods","html":"<table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Cost</th><th>Goods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1 CP</td><td>1 lb. of wheat</td></tr><tr><td>2 CP</td><td>1 lb. of flour, or one chicken</td></tr><tr><td>5 CP</td><td>1 lb. of salt</td></tr><tr><td>1 SP</td><td>1 lb. of iron, or 1 sq. yd. of canvas</td></tr><tr><td>5 SP</td><td>1 lb. of copper, or 1 sq. yd. of cotton cloth</td></tr><tr><td>1 GP</td><td>1 lb. of ginger, or one goat</td></tr><tr><td>2 GP</td><td>1 lb. of cinnamon or pepper, or one sheep</td></tr><tr><td>3 GP</td><td>1 lb. of cloves, or one pig</td></tr><tr><td>5 GP</td><td>1 lb. of silver, or 1 sq. yd. of linen</td></tr><tr><td>10 GP</td><td>1 sq. yd. of silk, or one cow</td></tr><tr><td>15 GP</td><td>1 lb. of saffron, or one ox</td></tr><tr><td>50 GP</td><td>1 lb. of gold</td></tr><tr><td>500 GP</td><td>1 lb. of platinum</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]},{"id":"items-magic-items","title":"Magic Items","html":""}]};
